---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const experiments = [
  "One geography",
  "A trusted local partner",
  "A small group of farmers",
  "A handful of investors",
  "Manual coordination using simple tools",
];

const success = [
  "Farmers feel supported rather than financially trapped.",
  "Investors gain enough transparency to participate with confidence.",
  "Local relationships become stronger instead of being replaced.",
  "Capital reaches farmers when it is actually needed.",
  "Repayment follows real agricultural cash flows.",
  "Trust grows through consistent execution rather than promises.",
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Farmer Capital Network · Sundharesan Kumaresan"
  description="A trusted way to coordinate capital, people, and execution around a farming season."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-6 pt-16 pb-16">
    <a href="/to" class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-text">&larr; To</a>

    <header class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">A venture</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-[12ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.98]" style="font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7.5vw, 5.2rem);">Farmer Capital Network</h1>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-[24ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.08]" style="font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3.8vw, 2.35rem);">A trusted way to coordinate capital, people, and execution around a farming season.</p>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>Agriculture isn't short of hardworking people. It is short of coordination.</p>
        <p>A farmer may need capital before sowing, quality inputs during the season, reliable logistics at harvest, and access to the right market at the right time. Investors, on the other hand, want to support agriculture but often lack visibility into where their money goes, how risks are managed, and who they can trust.</p>
        <p>I'm interested in exploring whether these two worlds can be connected through transparency, local relationships, and carefully designed workflows rather than another lending platform.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] md:border-t md:border-border md:pt-12">
      <div>
        <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">The problem</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>Most agricultural finance focuses on moving money.</p>
        <p>I'm more interested in helping complete successful farming seasons.</p>
        <p>Capital alone doesn't solve the problem if logistics fail, buyers disappear, prices change unexpectedly, or communication breaks down.</p>
        <p>The real challenge is coordinating many independent participants: farmers, investors, buyers, local operators, logistics providers, and support systems, so that each has the information and confidence to make better decisions.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 font-serif italic leading-[1.2] text-text" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3.8vw, 2.3rem);">Trust is the missing infrastructure.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] md:border-t md:border-border md:pt-12">
      <div>
        <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">The idea</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>The Farmer Capital Network is an exploration of what a trusted coordination layer could look like.</p>
        <p>Rather than treating financing as an isolated transaction, every production cycle becomes a shared workflow.</p>
        <p>A farmer receives timely support throughout the season. An investor gains visibility into how capital is being used. Local operators contribute ground-level verification and context.</p>
        <p>Repayment is connected to real agricultural events, such as milk collection or crop sales, instead of relying only on fixed repayment schedules disconnected from farming realities.</p>
        <p class="font-serif text-text" style="font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.9rem);">The long-term goal isn't simply to finance farms. It's to build a system where every participant can collaborate with greater confidence.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-5">
        <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold leading-[0.95]" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.2rem);">Why Start Small</h2>
        <span class="mb-4 h-px flex-1 bg-stellar"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[1fr_0.8fr]">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
          <p>Before building software, I want to understand how these relationships work in practice.</p>
          <p>The first experiments would likely be intentionally small. Every conversation, delay, success, and failure becomes an opportunity to learn.</p>
          <p>Only after understanding these workflows would software begin to replace repetitive operational work.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="border-t border-border">
          {experiments.map((item) => (
            <li class="border-b border-border py-4 text-text-muted">{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20">
      <h2 class="font-serif font-semibold" style="font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.95rem);">What Success Looks Like</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[60ch] text-text-muted">I'll consider the idea worth pursuing if I can demonstrate that:</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 border-t border-border" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
        {success.map((item) => (
          <li class="border-b border-border py-4 text-text-muted">{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-[0.75fr_1.25fr] md:border-t md:border-border md:pt-12">
      <div>
        <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">Relationship with iyal</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>This project is one of the first practical explorations within <a href="/iyal" class="font-script text-3xl leading-none text-accent transition-colors hover:text-accent-hover">iyal</a>.</p>
        <p>While iyal studies the broader questions of coordination, trust, and agricultural systems, the Farmer Capital Network focuses on one specific challenge: enabling trusted seasonal capital between farmers and those willing to support them.</p>
        <p>The lessons learned here may eventually shape a much broader platform, but this is where I'd like to begin.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 border-t-2 border-stellar pt-10">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-accent">Current Status</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[22ch] font-serif font-semibold leading-[1.05]" style="font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem);">Research and validation, conversation before software.</h2>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-[68ch] space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
        <p>This project is currently in the research and validation stage.</p>
        <p>I'm actively learning from farmers, investors, agricultural professionals, researchers, and anyone working close to the ecosystem. If this problem resonates with you, or if you think I'm approaching it the wrong way, I'd genuinely like to hear your perspective.</p>
        <p>The best ideas are usually shaped through conversation long before they're built.</p>
        <a href="mailto:sundharesansk11@gmail.com?subject=Farmer%20Capital%20Network" class="inline-block font-serif font-semibold leading-none text-text transition-colors hover:text-accent" style="font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.35rem);">Share your perspective <span class="text-accent">&rarr;</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-16" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
      <a href="/to" class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-text-muted transition-colors hover:text-text">&larr; To</a>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
